1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:00:06,330 --> 00:00:09,370
To the eighteen of you
who passed the first test...

4
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:13,210
First, congratulations on making it here.

5
00:00:14,030 --> 00:00:21,990
I hear people speculate all kinds of things
about my tests based on past results.

6
00:00:23,810 --> 00:00:27,630
I'm sure there are some of you
who have heard such rumors,

7
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:30,100
but you needn't prepare
yourselves for the worst.

8
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:33,220
The test is very simple.

9
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:38,310
Anyone who wishes to become a first-class
mage should be able to pass it with ease.

10
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:44,070
Now, allow me to explain
the details of the second test.

11
00:00:54,130 --> 00:00:58,050
<i>You're there like the wind</i>

12
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:02,680
<i>Closing your eyes at sunset</i>

13
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:08,310
<i>I wonder what's on your mind</i>

14
00:01:13,030 --> 00:01:17,030
<i>With your eyelids open</i>

15
00:01:17,030 --> 00:01:21,620
<i>Your eyes shone like glass</i>

16
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:28,370
<i>It faintly smelled like a sunny day</i>

17
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:39,510
<i>Clear up the sky, let flowers bloom</i>

18
00:01:39,510 --> 00:01:43,720
<i>Bloom and blame it on the sunny sky</i>

19
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:48,100
<i>Even the rain, when it stops</i>

20
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:53,110
<i>Will make you shine in the sunlight</i>

21
00:01:53,110 --> 00:01:58,490
<i>Calm the stirring sounds in my heart</i>

22
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:02,530
<i>We go like the sunny wind</i>

23
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:06,950
<i>Go on and fly over that cloud</i>

24
00:02:06,950 --> 00:02:11,790
<i>Further and further away</i>

25
00:02:19,070 --> 00:02:21,870
For the second test,
you will be raiding a dungeon.

26
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:26,130
You will raid the Ruins of the King's Tomb.

27
00:02:27,710 --> 00:02:33,900
There is only one condition for passing:
you must reach the deepest floor of the tomb.

28
00:02:35,310 --> 00:02:39,640
I am a pacifist. I dislike fighting.

29
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:43,540
Therefore, everyone who reaches
the bottom will pass.

30
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:44,630
Wait.

31
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:50,280
Many adventurers have failed to return
from this unexplored dungeon.

32
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:53,180
Are you planning to fail
all the test-takers again?

33
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:54,530
What are you talking about?

34
00:02:55,730 --> 00:02:59,430
You are attempting to reach
the pinnacle of magehood.

35
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:03,650
First-class mages make
the impossible possible.

36
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:09,030
You must forge ahead, regardless of whether
or not anyone's been there before you.

37
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:15,220
How should we prove we've reached the bottom?

38
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:18,020
Should we return with treasure?

39
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:20,500
You won't need to prove it.

40
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:23,660
I will descend to the bottom
of the dungeon with you.

41
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:27,070
Naturally, I will not be
assisting the test-takers.

42
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:32,250
Also, each of you will receive
one of these bottles.

43
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:39,150
It's an escape golem developed
by the first-class mage Lernen.

44
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,820
When the bottle is shattered,

45
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:45,530
the golem will manifest
and carry you out of the dungeon.

46
00:03:46,330 --> 00:03:49,250
They're still prototypes,
but they're safe enough.

47
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:52,230
Using your bottle means you fail the test,

48
00:03:52,230 --> 00:03:56,560
but I urge you to do so if you become unable
to continue due to injuries or otherwise.

49
00:03:57,030 --> 00:04:00,670
I have no intention of allowing mages
with promising futures to die here.

50
00:04:01,890 --> 00:04:06,500
Also, the bottles will shatter
automatically at dawn tomorrow.

51
00:04:07,470 --> 00:04:10,030
That is the time limit of the second test.

52
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,450
Now, let the test begin.

53
00:04:35,970 --> 00:04:38,230
There are multiple entrances.

54
00:04:38,230 --> 00:04:41,520
This seems to be a dungeon
of the Unified Dynasty.

55
00:04:41,890 --> 00:04:45,700
Dungeons of that era have multiple entrances,

56
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:48,530
but they all lead to the deepest level.

57
00:04:48,530 --> 00:04:50,740
Examining the entrances should allow us

58
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:53,780
to determine the internal
structure of the dungeon.

59
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:56,290
The group should split up and—

60
00:04:56,290 --> 00:04:59,040
Why are you acting like
we're working together?

61
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:08,040
There's no reason for us to fight this time.

62
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:11,310
It's better for all of us to cooperate.

63
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:13,570
I can't agree to that.

64
00:05:15,590 --> 00:05:20,060
Unlike in the first test, our companions'
survival isn't a condition for passing the test.

65
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:23,560
We're not obligated to help each other,

66
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:27,570
and we even risk becoming someone's
sacrificial pawn if the need arises.

67
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:32,060
You in particular seem
knowledgeable about dungeons.

68
00:05:33,470 --> 00:05:35,190
I'm going alone.

69
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:52,180
We're all carrying baggage from the first test.

70
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:55,840
At the very least, I can't work
with anyone I don't know well.

71
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:00,280
Let's go.

72
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:04,420
Wait for me.

73
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:13,690
Those fools. Why don't they realize
working together is better?

74
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:15,850
Let's go, Fern.

75
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,590
Are you sure, Ms. Frieren?

76
00:06:19,050 --> 00:06:22,890
There's no chance of everyone
working together anymore.

77
00:06:28,450 --> 00:06:29,960
I see.

78
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:33,940
I shall accompany your group.

79
00:06:35,030 --> 00:06:38,970
You seem like you'll have the
safest time reaching the bottom.

80
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:41,920
You'd better not interfere.

81
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:45,920
I shall neither interfere nor assist you.

82
00:06:53,530 --> 00:06:56,240
This is the safest route.

83
00:06:58,570 --> 00:07:01,460
We'll proceed with caution
while mapping the dungeon.

84
00:07:14,010 --> 00:07:17,560
The floor there is trapped. Be careful.

85
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:26,600
You always know so much about dungeons.

86
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:30,160
I didn't always.

87
00:07:31,530 --> 00:07:33,900
It was Himmel who loved dungeons.

88
00:07:34,650 --> 00:07:38,210
We entered so many of them
to hunt down monsters.

89
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:42,570
What do you mean, he loved dungeons?

90
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,090
It's exactly what it sounds like.

91
00:07:45,470 --> 00:07:47,360
He said they excited him.

92
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:50,070
It doesn't make sense, does it?

93
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:56,730
These stairs lead to the next floor.

94
00:07:58,490 --> 00:08:01,620
I see. Then we chose the wrong route.

95
00:08:02,210 --> 00:08:04,700
Let's head back to the last branch.

96
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:06,080
Indeed.

97
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:11,920
Why? We're looking for the monster
at the bottom of the dungeon.

98
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:15,240
When will you learn, Eisen?

99
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:21,670
In a dungeon, one must explore the entire
floor before proceeding to the next one.

100
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:23,640
Every adventurer knows that.

101
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:25,320
I've never heard that before.

102
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:29,260
You think I'm being foolish, don't you?

103
00:08:31,430 --> 00:08:35,410
But isn't it best to be able to have fun
while helping people?

104
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:38,320
It won't always be like this.

105
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:41,100
As we travel, the dungeons will
become more life-threatening.

106
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:42,530
That's right.

107
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:45,070
I intend to enjoy it until the end.

108
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:48,770
I'll have fun adventuring, raiding dungeons,

109
00:08:48,770 --> 00:08:51,760
defeating monsters, finding treasure,

110
00:08:52,150 --> 00:08:54,770
and before I know it,
I'll have saved the world.

111
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:58,510
That's the kind of adventure I want to have.

112
00:09:00,110 --> 00:09:01,200
Besides...

113
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:06,540
There might be a rare grimoire
down the path left untraveled.

114
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,450
What are you doing? Let's hurry back.

115
00:09:09,450 --> 00:09:10,550
What?

116
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:14,710
It really doesn't make sense, does it?

117
00:09:28,070 --> 00:09:30,050
Kanne, let's go.

118
00:09:43,470 --> 00:09:46,220
In the end, only the five of us stayed.

119
00:09:46,950 --> 00:09:50,510
We could've beaten the dungeon easily

120
00:09:50,510 --> 00:09:53,500
if we'd all worked together
and assigned roles.

121
00:09:54,350 --> 00:09:58,250
We had enough skilled mages to make it happen.

122
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:02,890
Denken, not everyone is as pragmatic as you.

123
00:10:03,490 --> 00:10:07,220
It's like what you said
toward the end of the first test.

124
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,760
It must not have sat right with them.

125
00:10:13,350 --> 00:10:17,350
Think of it this way:
only the smartest have remained.

126
00:10:17,970 --> 00:10:20,130
At the very least,

127
00:10:20,130 --> 00:10:24,790
there aren't any idiots here to hold us back
by falling for simple traps like mimics.

128
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:27,280
Isn't that good enough, Denken?

129
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:31,690
I doubt anyone that foolish would
be taking this test to begin with.

130
00:10:32,770 --> 00:10:34,190
Let's go.

131
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:45,330
This mana...

132
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:48,020
It might be a grimoire.

133
00:10:48,550 --> 00:10:52,550
Ms. Frieren, you saw the results
of that Mikheit spell.

134
00:10:53,950 --> 00:10:55,370
It's a mimic.

135
00:10:56,450 --> 00:11:01,330
Fern, that spell is only 99% accurate.

136
00:11:01,330 --> 00:11:03,450
And what if it is?

137
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:11,310
Historical discoveries have been made by
great mages who recognized that remaining 1%.

138
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:18,210
It's just as I thought.

139
00:11:19,910 --> 00:11:22,690
There's a valuable grimoire inside here.

140
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:27,620
That's what my experience
as a mage is telling me.

141
00:11:33,410 --> 00:11:36,980
It's dark and scary in here!

142
00:11:38,310 --> 00:11:39,860
It's dark! I'm scared!

143
00:11:41,270 --> 00:11:42,870
It's dark and scary!

144
00:11:56,190 --> 00:11:59,500
<i>Maybe I chose the wrong people to follow.</i>

145
00:12:09,090 --> 00:12:11,480
Don't step on the floor in the center.

146
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,850
The ceiling will come crashing down on you.

147
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:19,930
Is that person-shaped stain there...

148
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:23,940
Brutal. It doesn't even leave bones behind.

149
00:12:45,090 --> 00:12:46,380
Gargoyles!

150
00:13:44,710 --> 00:13:47,030
Denken, someone got trapped.

151
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:47,990
I know.

152
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:50,240
She's on the other side of the wall.

153
00:13:51,730 --> 00:13:53,340
Stand back.

154
00:14:00,330 --> 00:14:01,830
It didn't work.

155
00:14:02,370 --> 00:14:03,580
Then we have no choice.

156
00:14:03,850 --> 00:14:05,330
Break your bottle!

157
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:23,730
Wow.

158
00:14:23,730 --> 00:14:26,370
We're already down another test-taker.

159
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:32,860
Letting your guard down for a moment
here could cost you your life.

160
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:37,230
So these are the Ruins of the King's Tomb.

161
00:14:47,830 --> 00:14:50,760
Hey, Fern. Can I make a suggestion?

162
00:14:51,190 --> 00:14:54,270
Stop pulling. You're going to rip me in half.

163
00:14:54,950 --> 00:14:55,800
Okay.

164
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:01,160
To save someone from a mimic,
you should push in instead.

165
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:04,060
It makes the mimic choke and stop biting.

166
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:07,900
Is it a dog or something?

167
00:15:10,950 --> 00:15:13,080
I'm safe.

168
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:15,530
Honestly.

169
00:15:15,970 --> 00:15:19,040
How did you get out of those
when you were by yourself?

170
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:22,240
By blowing them up from the inside
with offensive magic.

171
00:15:23,050 --> 00:15:26,920
But I don't like to do it
since it makes my hair frizz up.

172
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:28,040
I'm back.

173
00:15:28,570 --> 00:15:30,770
I have ringlets now.

174
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:35,860
So that's why you'd sometimes
have a different hairstyle.

175
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:36,860
Why?

176
00:15:37,870 --> 00:15:42,550
Let's pull ourselves together and keep going.

177
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:52,110
Gargoyles.

178
00:15:52,630 --> 00:15:54,600
We'll defeat them before they start moving.

179
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:01,870
We've been seeing these
medals all over the place.

180
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:04,670
Apparently some dilettante collects them.

181
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:12,670
This looks like the main route.
Let's turn back.

182
00:16:12,670 --> 00:16:13,560
Why?

183
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,960
We're progressing more
smoothly than I expected.

184
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:24,470
It does seem a bit odd
for an unexplored dungeon.

185
00:16:24,470 --> 00:16:27,710
Judging by its construction,
we should be nearing the bottom, too.

186
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:30,960
Either way, don't let your guard down.

187
00:16:31,530 --> 00:16:34,970
Let's take a break in the
next burial chamber we find.

188
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:40,720
We've acquired some pretty nice stuff.

189
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,880
It just looks like junk to me.

190
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:44,870
Huh.

191
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:50,220
I don't get it.

192
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:51,470
Neither do I.

193
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,910
Why do those things make her happy?

194
00:16:56,650 --> 00:16:58,170
She's rubbing it on her cheek.

195
00:17:00,070 --> 00:17:03,060
You're the one I don't understand, Fern.

196
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:08,600
I've never seen a mage
as skilled as you at your age.

197
00:17:09,170 --> 00:17:11,560
You must have trained rather hard.

198
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:15,700
And yet I sense no passion
or determination in you.

199
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:17,100
You're a strange girl.

200
00:17:20,950 --> 00:17:26,450
I became a proper mage
to repay a debt to someone.

201
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:32,460
That was my life's goal at the time.

202
00:17:33,580 --> 00:17:35,200
I devoted all my effort to achieving it

203
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:38,480
without considering anything
that would come after that.

204
00:17:40,890 --> 00:17:46,960
I must've used up all my passion
and determination then.

205
00:17:48,470 --> 00:17:52,620
Then why do you continue
searching for magic?

206
00:17:55,810 --> 00:17:58,610
Ms. Frieren seems to be
having fun, doesn't she?

207
00:17:58,610 --> 00:17:59,750
Yes.

208
00:18:01,050 --> 00:18:03,860
The first time I entered a dungeon,

209
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:10,350
Ms. Frieren joyfully smiled
while collecting magic junk.

210
00:18:15,670 --> 00:18:17,800
It made me smile, too.

211
00:18:18,530 --> 00:18:26,120
I think I continue searching for magic
because I like seeing her happy.

212
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:31,880
We should get going.

213
00:18:36,950 --> 00:18:40,570
Looks like I was right
to follow you after all.

214
00:18:41,140 --> 00:18:46,080
I'm sure you can enjoy
even this brutal dungeon.

215
00:19:10,310 --> 00:19:12,040
The atmosphere has changed.

216
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:15,470
Maybe we're near the bottom.

217
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,300
Wirbel.

218
00:19:19,730 --> 00:19:21,830
What? Can't walk any—

219
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:23,540
I'm restrained.

220
00:19:23,540 --> 00:19:26,400
There are three mages concealing their mana.

221
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:27,910
It's an ambush.

222
00:19:27,910 --> 00:19:29,040
Oh?

223
00:19:33,570 --> 00:19:35,340
Scharf, block their vision.

224
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:37,960
The spell cast on Ehre is Sorganeil.

225
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:39,010
I know.

226
00:19:54,510 --> 00:19:58,560
No wonder the Ruins of the King's Tomb
have never been conquered.

227
00:20:00,090 --> 00:20:04,130
I wasn't expecting to encounter these here.

228
00:20:05,910 --> 00:20:07,330
Scharf, you're on me.

229
00:20:07,610 --> 00:20:09,580
Ehre, you're on Scharf.

230
00:20:09,870 --> 00:20:11,870
And I'll take on Ehre.

231
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:14,970
Let's do this.

232
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:58,990
It's a replica made using magic.

233
00:20:59,730 --> 00:21:02,480
It must be the work of demons or monsters.

234
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:08,780
But I've never seen such a perfect copy
of another person before.

235
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:12,290
Its mana and skills were
the same as yours, Laufen.

236
00:21:13,190 --> 00:21:14,980
So was its behavior.

237
00:21:14,980 --> 00:21:18,390
It's possible even our memories were used.

238
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:21,690
I don't like this.

239
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:27,610
The one saving grace is that it's
instantly recognizable as a fake.

240
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:31,920
At the very least, there's no danger
of us attacking each other.

241
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:38,050
If whoever cast this spell can control
multiple copies simultaneously,

242
00:21:38,050 --> 00:21:40,570
they must be terrifyingly powerful.

243
00:21:43,070 --> 00:21:47,210
Either way, we were right to team up.

244
00:21:50,750 --> 00:21:53,540
It gives us more options
for dealing with them.

245
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:22,080
Denken, can we deal with that, too?

246
00:22:27,970 --> 00:22:32,790
The one thing I can say
is that if this weren't a test,

247
00:22:32,790 --> 00:22:35,820
I would've shattered my bottle
a long time ago.

248
00:22:50,030 --> 00:22:53,160
<i>And I'm alright</i>

249
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:56,080
<i>Yeah, I hear you</i>

250
00:22:56,080 --> 00:23:01,670
<i>The wind teases this hair that's longer now</i>

251
00:23:01,670 --> 00:23:04,090
<i>There's meaning in everything</i>

252
00:23:04,590 --> 00:23:07,090
<i>Even the days that came to a halt</i>

253
00:23:07,670 --> 00:23:13,720
<i>Now that I finally understand,
I've caught up to you</i>

254
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:17,520
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

255
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:20,390
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

256
00:23:20,390 --> 00:23:25,070
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

257
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:31,320
<i>I won't ask to see you, so at least</i>

258
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:37,080
<i>Let me remember the past, just for today</i>

259
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:43,080
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

260
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:48,960
<i>No more hesitations, I'd choose the present</i>

261
00:23:50,050 --> 00:23:53,010
<i>Anytime, anywhere, yah</i>

262
00:23:53,010 --> 00:23:57,640
<i>Anytime, anywhere</i>

263
00:23:57,640 --> 00:24:00,640
<i>I'll be there (close your eyes,
and I'll always be there)</i>

264
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:03,400
<i>Even if there are no absolutes</i>

265
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:06,440
<i>I'm always aware of your thoughts</i>

266
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:12,490
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

267
00:24:12,950 --> 00:24:19,410
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby
for you to come back home</i>

268
00:24:20,330 --> 00:24:23,790
Now then, what are we going to do about this?

269
00:24:20,870 --> 00:24:22,210
Smells nice.

270
00:24:21,320 --> 00:24:23,060
It's time.

271
00:24:22,340 --> 00:24:24,140
If we're evenly matched,

272
00:24:23,830 --> 00:24:25,020
That's not funny.

273
00:24:24,140 --> 00:24:26,280
then who wins will come down to luck.

274
00:24:24,330 --> 00:24:26,420
Could you please look into my eyes?

275
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:27,690
So it's not impossible.

276
00:24:26,310 --> 00:24:28,120
How much time do you need?

277
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:30,050
They're perfect replicas.
